# One line ending everywhere: LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the machines this is worked on, which stores LF and
# checks out CRLF. Harmless in itself, but it means a file written by a tool (LF)
# and the same file after a checkout (CRLF) differ byte for byte -- which breaks
# any md5 or sha verification of a deployed copy, makes every checkout look like
# it changed every file, and would make the SDK provenance hash in
# sdk/SDK-VERSION.json disagree with itself on a different machine.
#
# LF is also what is served: the harness runs from a static web root, and the
# modules run inside REDCap on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf


# Binary, and not to be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
